r former governor, against Republican Michael Whatley, the RNC chair. With Thom Tillis retiring, Democrats see a top flip opportunity in a state that leans slightly Republican but has repeatedly elected Cooper statewide.\n\nPolling since mid-September consistently shows Cooper up by roughly nine to ten points, including surveys from Republican-leaning firms. Cooper has dramatically out-raised Whatley, whose campaign faces cash shortfalls despite outside support. Expert raters nearly all call the race Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Cooper's chances around 95 percent. The main question is the size of the margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9425, "margin": 7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.93, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9375, "margin": 8.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9346, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9278, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9264, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.939, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9386, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9577, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9512, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9379, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9381, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.956, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9414, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9393, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9452, "margin": 9.2}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.965, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.965, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.9374, "margin": 9.